      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Structure-of-Arrays layout: separate arrays for each coordinate and velocity.\n */\ntypedef struct {\n    float *x, *y, *z;\n    float *vx, *vy, *vz;\n} Bodies;\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system. Uses tiling on both i and j loops for cache locality.\n */\nvoid body_force(Bodies p, float dt, int n) {\n    const int IBLOCK = 8;\n    const int JBLOCK = 128;\n\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int ii = 0; ii < n; ii += IBLOCK) {\n        int i_end = ii + IBLOCK;\n        if (i_end > n) i_end = n;\n\n        // Local accumulators for each body in the block\n        float fx[IBLOCK], fy[IBLOCK], fz[IBLOCK];\n        for (int ib = 0; ib < i_end - ii; ++ib) {\n            fx[ib] = 0.0f;\n            fy[ib] = 0.0f;\n            fz[ib] = 0.0f;\n        }\n\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < n; jj += JBLOCK) {\n            int j_end = jj + JBLOCK;\n            if (j_end > n) j_end = n;\n\n            // Process all pairs in this tile\n            for (int ib = ii; ib < i_end; ++ib) {\n                float pix = p.x[ib];\n                float piy = p.y[ib];\n                float piz = p.z[ib];\n                int idx = ib - ii;\n                float fxx = fx[idx], fyy = fy[idx], fzz = fz[idx];\n\n                for (int jb = jj; jb < j_end; ++jb) {\n                    float dx = p.x[jb] - pix;\n                    float dy = p.y[jb] - piy;\n                    float dz = p.z[jb] - piz;\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n                    fxx += dx * inv_dist3;\n                    fyy += dy * inv_dist3;\n                    fzz += dz * inv_dist3;\n                }\n\n                fx[idx] = fxx;\n                fy[idx] = fyy;\n                fz[idx] = fzz;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Update velocities for this block\n        for (int ib = ii; ib < i_end; ++ib) {\n            int idx = ib - ii;\n            p.vx[ib] += dt * fx[idx];\n            p.vy[ib] += dt * fy[idx];\n            p.vz[ib] += dt * fz[idx];\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initialized bodies.\n */\nBodies read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n    int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n    if (b != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    Bodies bodies;\n    int n = *nbodies;\n    bodies.x = (float *)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    bodies.y = (float *)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    bodies.z = (float *)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    bodies.vx = (float *)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    bodies.vy = (float *)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    bodies.vz = (float *)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n\n    // Read interleaved AoS data and convert to SoA\n    float *tmp = (float *)malloc(6 * n * sizeof(float));\n    b = fread(tmp, 6 * n * sizeof(float), 1, stdin);\n    if (b != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        bodies.x[i] = tmp[6*i + 0];\n        bodies.y[i] = tmp[6*i + 1];\n        bodies.z[i] = tmp[6*i + 2];\n        bodies.vx[i] = tmp[6*i + 3];\n        bodies.vy[i] = tmp[6*i + 4];\n        bodies.vz[i] = tmp[6*i + 5];\n    }\n\n    free(tmp);\n    return bodies;\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset (AoS format).\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Bodies bodies) {\n    float *tmp = (float *)malloc(6 * nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        tmp[6*i + 0] = bodies.x[i];\n        tmp[6*i + 1] = bodies.y[i];\n        tmp[6*i + 2] = bodies.z[i];\n        tmp[6*i + 3] = bodies.vx[i];\n        tmp[6*i + 4] = bodies.vy[i];\n        tmp[6*i + 5] = bodies.vz[i];\n    }\n\n    int b = fwrite(tmp, nbodies * sizeof(float) * 6, 1, stdout);\n    if (b != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    free(tmp);\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n    int nbodies;\n\n    Bodies bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n    /*\n     * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\n     * and bodies' positions are integrated.\n     */\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\n        body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\n            bodies.x[i] += bodies.vx[i] * DT;\n            bodies.y[i] += bodies.vy[i] * DT;\n            bodies.z[i] += bodies.vz[i] * DT;\n        }\n    }\n\n    write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n    free(bodies.x);\n    free(bodies.y);\n    free(bodies.z);\n    free(bodies.vx);\n    free(bodies.vy);\n    free(bodies.vz);\n\n    exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Converting the data layout from Array-of-Structures (AoS) to Structure-of-Arrays (SoA) improves spatial locality when accessing coordinates across bodies. Applying tiling on both i-loop (block size 8) and j-loop (block size 128) further enhances cache reuse: each loaded body coordinate in a j-block is reused for all bodies in the current i-block, reducing memory traffic. OpenMP parallelization over i-blocks exploits all four cores while preserving per-body accumulation order (j indices processed sequentially), ensuring bit-exact results.",
  "notes": "Changed Body struct to separate arrays for x,y,z,vx,vy,vz. Added tiling with IBLOCK=8 and JBLOCK=128. Used OpenMP parallel for over i-blocks. Input/output conversion between AoS (binary format) and SoA is done in read_dataset/write_dataset using temporary buffer. The force accumulation order per body remains increasing j due to sequential processing of j-blocks, preserving floating-point exactness.",
